{"matches":[{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-58c5-g7wp-6w37","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-58c5-g7wp-6w37","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/angular/angular/security/advisories/GHSA-58c5-g7wp-6w37","https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/0276479e7d0e280e0f8d26fa567d3b7aa97a516f","https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/05fe6686a97fa0bcd3cf157805b3612033f975bc","https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/3240d856d942727372a705252f7c8c115394a41e","https://github.com/angular/angular/releases/tag/19.2.16","https://github.com/angular/angular/releases/tag/20.3.14","https://github.com/angular/angular/releases/tag/21.0.1","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-66035"],"description":"Angular is Vulnerable to XSRF Token Leakage via Protocol-Relative URLs in Angular HTTP Client","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:N/SA:N","metrics":{"baseScore":7.7},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66035","epss":0.00098,"percentile":0.27008,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66035","cwe":"CWE-201","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2025-66035","cwe":"CWE-359","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["19.2.16"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"19.2.16","date":"2025-11-27","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.07448},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2025-66035","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-66035","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/0276479e7d0e280e0f8d26fa567d3b7aa97a516f","https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/05fe6686a97fa0bcd3cf157805b3612033f975bc","https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/3240d856d942727372a705252f7c8c115394a41e","https://github.com/angular/angular/releases/tag/19.2.16","https://github.com/angular/angular/releases/tag/20.3.14","https://github.com/angular/angular/releases/tag/21.0.1","https://github.com/angular/angular/security/advisories/GHSA-58c5-g7wp-6w37"],"description":"Angular is a development platform for building mobile and desktop web applications using TypeScript/JavaScript and other languages. Prior to versions 19.2.16, 20.3.14, and 21.0.1, there is a XSRF token leakage via protocol-relative URLs in angular HTTP clients. The vulnerability is a Credential Leak by App Logic that leads to the unauthorized disclosure of the Cross-Site Request Forgery (XSRF) token to an attacker-controlled domain. Angular's HttpClient has a built-in XSRF protection mechanism that works by checking if a request URL starts with a protocol (http:// or https://) to determine if it is cross-origin. If the URL starts with protocol-relative URL (//), it is incorrectly treated as a same-origin request, and the XSRF token is automatically added to the X-XSRF-TOKEN header. This issue has been patched in versions 19.2.16, 20.3.14, and 21.0.1. A workaround for this issue involves avoiding using protocol-relative URLs (URLs starting with //) in HttpClient requests. All backend communication URLs should be hardcoded as relative paths (starting with a single /) or fully qualified, trusted absolute URLs.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":7.7},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66035","epss":0.00098,"percentile":0.27008,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66035","cwe":"CWE-201","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2025-66035","cwe":"CWE-359","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"@angular/common","version":"11.2.14"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-58c5-g7wp-6w37","versionConstraint":"<19.2.16 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"19.2.16"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/%40angular/common@11.2.14?package-id=2e93faa441ba3cf1","name":"@angular/common","version":"11.2.14","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/nifi-registry/nifi-registry-core/nifi-registry-web-ui/src/main/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":[],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:\\@angular\\/common:\\@angular\\/common:11.2.14:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/%40angular/common@11.2.14","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-v4hv-rgfq-gp49","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v4hv-rgfq-gp49","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/angular/angular/security/advisories/GHSA-v4hv-rgfq-gp49","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-66412","https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/1c6b0704fb63d051fab8acff84d076abfbc4893a"],"description":"Angular Stored XSS Vulnerability via SVG Animation, SVG URL and MathML Attributes","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","metrics":{"baseScore":8.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66412","epss":0.00039,"percentile":0.11625,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66412","cwe":"CWE-79","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":[],"state":"not-fixed"},"advisories":[],"risk":0.0312},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2025-66412","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-66412","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/1c6b0704fb63d051fab8acff84d076abfbc4893a","https://github.com/angular/angular/security/advisories/GHSA-v4hv-rgfq-gp49"],"description":"Angular is a development platform for building mobile and desktop web applications using TypeScript/JavaScript and other languages. Prior to 21.0.2, 20.3.15, and 19.2.17, A Stored Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability has been identified in the Angular Template Compiler. It occurs because the compiler's internal security schema is incomplete, allowing attackers to bypass Angular's built-in security sanitization. Specifically, the schema fails to classify certain URL-holding attributes (e.g., those that could contain javascript: URLs) as requiring strict URL security, enabling the injection of malicious scripts. This vulnerability is fixed in 21.0.2, 20.3.15, and 19.2.17.","cvss":[{"source":"nvd@nist.gov","type":"Primary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.4,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":2.8},"vendorMetadata":{}},{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:A/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":8.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66412","epss":0.00039,"percentile":0.11625,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2025-66412","cwe":"CWE-79","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"@angular/compiler","version":"11.2.14"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-v4hv-rgfq-gp49","versionConstraint":"<=18.2.14 (semantic)"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/%40angular/compiler@11.2.14?package-id=4b1f0eb0191eaddc","name":"@angular/compiler","version":"11.2.14","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/nifi-registry/nifi-registry-core/nifi-registry-web-ui/src/main/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","license